{{$NEXT}}

 - extract_and_wait and agent_and_wait now fail a job that starts without an id
   with a WWW::Firecrawl::Error of type api and the failure spec 'firecrawl',
   like the other flow helpers, instead of a bare string.
 - The runtime dependencies now list every module the code loads, including
   Future::Utils for the poll loops, so an installation from the cpanfile is
   complete.
 - The constructor now accepts the retry and classification settings the
   documentation always listed (max_attempts, retry_backoff, retry_statuses,
   on_retry, is_failure, failure_codes, strict) and hands them to
   WWW::Firecrawl instead of croaking on them. Combining them with a
   prebuilt firecrawl instance croaks.

0.001     2026-04-18 03:35:07Z

 - Initial release
 - IO::Async / Net::Async::HTTP client wrapping WWW::Firecrawl
 - Future-returning equivalents of all v2 endpoints
 - Retry on transport + retryable API errors via delay_future
 - Flow helpers: crawl_and_collect, batch_scrape_and_wait, extract_and_wait, agent_and_wait
 - scrape_many (partial-success, concurrent) and retry_failed_pages
 - Flow results carry {data, failed, raw_data, stats} split by is_failure policy
